WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.800
We’re eating more fish than ever these days.
如今，我们吃的鱼比以往任何时候都多。

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:11.760
At around 20 kilograms per person, global fish consumption is now more than twice what it was in the 1960s.
全球鱼类消费量现已达到人均约20千克，是20世纪60年代的两倍多。

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:16.070
What’s really remarkable, though, is where that fish comes from.
不过，真正引人注目的是这些鱼从哪里来。

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:22.920
For the first time in human history, most of our aquatic food now comes from farming rather than fishing.
如今，我们的水产食品大部分来自养殖，而非捕捞，这在人类历史上尚属首次。

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:32.550
People ate around 73 million tonnes of farmed fish—just more than half of the volume of fish that humans consumed—in 2014.
2014年，人们吃掉了约7300万吨养殖鱼，略多于人类当年鱼类消费总量的一半。

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:43.500
That’s out of a total fish supply of 167 million tonnes; the remaining 20 million or so tonnes go into things like animal feed and medical products.
鱼类总供应量为1.67亿吨，人类消费的鱼就出自其中；其余2000万吨左右则用来制作动物饲料、医疗产品等。

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.980
To keep eating fish at the current rate, we’re definitely going to need to keep aquaculture developing.
要按目前的速度继续吃鱼，我们肯定需要让水产养殖持续发展。

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:55.880
That’s because the volume of fish caught in the wild has leveled off since the 1990s.
这是因为自20世纪90年代以来，野外捕捞的鱼量就已趋于平稳。

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:02.030
Back in 1974, only 10% of marine fish stocks had been overfished.
1974年时，只有10%的海洋鱼类种群遭到了过度捕捞。

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.370
Now, more than three-tenths are.
如今，这一比例已超过十分之三。

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:10.320
Only a tenth of our oceans’ fish stocks could sustain heavier fishing than current levels.
我们海洋里的鱼类种群中，只有十分之一能承受高于目前水平的捕捞强度。

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.810
But while catches at sea have suffered, fish-farming has been growing at a fast rate.
但是，尽管海上捕捞量受到了冲击，鱼类养殖却一直在快速增长。

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.850
A lot of that is coming from China, which produces 60% of the world’s farmed fish.
这一增长很大一部分来自中国，中国的养殖鱼产量占全世界的60%。

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:29.380
In fact, some 35 countries, including China, now produce more farmed than wild-caught fish.
事实上，如今包括中国在内约有35个国家，养殖鱼产量高于野生捕捞鱼产量。

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:38.730
This shift toward aquaculture isn’t just good for ensuring salmon on your plate; it’s also crucial to ensuring food security and sustainability.
这种向水产养殖的转变不仅有利于确保你的餐盘里有三文鱼，对保障粮食安全和可持续性也至关重要。

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:45.100
By 2050, the world will need to feed an estimated 9.7 billion people.
到2050年，世界需要养活的人口估计将达到97亿。

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.970
They’ll have to get their protein somewhere.
他们总得从某个地方获取蛋白质。

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:55.280
However, raising cattle, pigs, and other land-based animals requires vast amounts of grain and water.
然而，饲养牛、猪等陆生动物需要大量的谷物和水。

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:04.600
For example, pound for pound, beef requires 15 times more feed to raise than carp, a freshwater fish farmed all over Asia.
例如，养出同等重量的牛肉和鲤鱼，前者所需的饲料是后者的15倍；鲤鱼是一种在亚洲各地都有养殖的淡水鱼。

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:10.650
That grain—and the water needed to grow it—could be consumed by people instead.
这些谷物，连同种植谷物所需的水，本可以转而供人类消费。

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.980
However, aquaculture is no silver bullet.
然而，水产养殖并非万全之策。

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.840
In some Southeast Asian countries, shrimp farming does disastrous damage to marine ecosystems.
在一些东南亚国家，养虾业对海洋生态系统造成灾难性的破坏。

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:27.690
Despite these problems, however, shrimp continues to be among the most popular seafoods worldwide.
然而，尽管存在这些问题，虾仍然是全世界最受欢迎的海鲜之一。
